# Local development only. Copy to .env.local.
#
# Deployed builds never read this file — .dockerignore excludes .env*, so no env
# file reaches the image. There the same two values arrive as Docker build args
# and the build fails if either is missing. See the Dockerfile.

# Which backend to call. Left unset the app falls back to the STAGING backend
# (see src/lib/api/client.ts), which is usually what you want when working on
# the UI alone. Point it at the backend repo running on this machine to work on
# both at once.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Which Supabase project signs users in — the same value as SUPABASE_URL in
# OJT-system-BE/.env. Prod and staging are separate Supabase projects, so this
# decides whose auth.users you are authenticated against, and getting it wrong
# is not cosmetic.
#
# Not a secret: it is the address the browser is sent to and it ships in every
# build.
#
# The origin you serve from must also be on that project's redirect allow-list,
# or Google sends people back with an error.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
